# Developing custom Apps in Metric Insights
The Metric Insights platform can be used for the deployment of custom Apps (also called Portal Pages).
Local development of these Portal Pages requires pp-dev and knowledge of App (Portal Page) Variables (a feature within the Metric Insights platform).

# pp-dev: local development of a Portal Page

[`@metricinsights/pp-dev`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@metricinsights/pp-dev) is the development framework and build tool for Portal Pages (custom Apps). It runs the page locally (Vite, or Next.js through `pp-dev next`), proxies API requests to a Metric Insights instance with the developer's token, loads the page's template variables, syncs the built template back to MI and zips the build for upload. This is a summary for pp-dev 1.5; the reference is the package README, https://github.com/mi-examples/pp-dev#readme, which wins when the two disagree.

## Scripts and commands

Projects created with `npm create @metricinsights/pp-dev` already have the scripts:

| Script    | Vite templates (`vanilla`, `vanilla-ts`, `react`)            | Next.js templates   |
| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------- |
| `dev`     | `pp-dev`                                                     | `pp-dev next`       |
| `build`   | `pp-dev build` (TypeScript templates: `tsc && pp-dev build`) | `pp-dev next-build` |
| `preview` | `pp-dev preview` (react)                                     | —                   |

CLI commands: `pp-dev [root]` (aliases `dev`, `serve`), `pp-dev next [root]` (`next-serve`, `next-dev`), `pp-dev build [root]`, `pp-dev next-build [root]`, `pp-dev preview [root]`, `pp-dev optimize [root]`, `pp-dev migrate [config]`, `pp-dev changelog [old] [new]`, `pp-dev generate-icon-font [source] [destination]` (needs `svgtofont` in the project since pp-dev 1.5.1: `npm install --save-dev svgtofont`).

Global options: `-c, --config <file>`, `--base <path>`, `-l, --logLevel <info|warn|error|silent>`, `--clearScreen`, `--mode <development|production|test>`. Dev-server options: `--host [host]` (a bare `--host` listens on all addresses), `--port <port>` (default `3000`); `--open [path]` and `--strictPort` apply to `pp-dev` only. `pp-dev --help` and `pp-dev <command> --help` list everything.

## Configuration

The config lives in `pp-dev.config.ts` (or `.js`, `.cjs`, `.mjs`, `.json`), or under the `pp-dev` key of `package.json`. Use `defineConfig()` for typing. The config is grouped:

```typescript
// pp-dev.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from '@metricinsights/pp-dev';

export default defineConfig({
  mi: {
    url: 'https://mi.company.com',
    mode: 'standalone',
    apiVersion: 7,
  },
  app: {
    id: 1,
    type: 'template',
  },
});
```

| Section     | Fields (default)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `mi`        | `url`; `token` (`MI_ACCESS_TOKEN` env; keep it in `.env`, never in the config); `mode: 'standalone' \| 'embedding'` (`standalone` hides the MI navigation, `embedding` keeps it); `include: 'top-bar' \| 'shared-components'` (standalone only); `apiVersion: 6 \| 7` (`7`) |
| `app`       | `id` (the Portal Page id, required for `type: 'template'`); `type: 'template' \| 'page'` (`template` syncs back to MI); `name` (`package.json#name`)                                                                                                                       |
| `proxy`     | `cache` (`true`); `cacheTtl` (`600000` ms); `tls.allowSelfSigned` (`false`, MI requests only)                                                                                                                                                                              |
| `build`     | `outDir` (`'dist'`); `zip` (`true` or `{ fileName, outDir, inDir }`); `versionFile` (`true`); `imageOptimisations` (`true`)                                                                                                                                                |
| `sync`      | `backupsDir` (`'backups'`); `maxBackups` (`20`, `false` keeps all); `buildTimeoutMs` (`600000`)                                                                                                                                                                            |
| `inspector` | `enabled` (`true`); `maxMemory` (`104857600`, 100 MB); `captureLimit` (`10485760`, 10 MB)                                                                                                                                                                                   |
| `devPanel`  | `position` (`'bottom-right'`); `hidden` (`false`); `autoHide` (`false`)                                                                                                                                                                                                    |
| `users`     | `persist` (`false`): keep the users added with an API token between runs, in `~/.pp-dev/users/`                                                                                                                                                                             |
| `server`    | `allowedHosts` (`[]`): host names the dev server answers besides `localhost`, `*.localhost` and IP addresses, for tunnels; `true` answers any host, avoid it                                                                                                                |

Validation: `mi.include` needs `mi.mode: 'standalone'`; `mi.url` is required when `mi.mode` is `embedding` or `app.type` is `template`; `app.id` is required for `app.type: 'template'` (and for `page` in `standalone` mode).

Environment: `MI_ACCESS_TOKEN` (default for `mi.token`), `PP_DEV_DIST_ZIP`, `PP_DEV_DIST_ZIP_DIR`, `PP_DEV_DIST_ZIP_FILENAME`, `PP_DEV_VERSION_MANIFEST`, `PP_DEV_VERSION_FILE_TEMPLATE`. The `.env*` files of the project root are loaded (variables prefixed `MI_`); the generated `.gitignore` keeps them out of git.

A config in the 0.x flat format (`backendBaseURL`, `portalPageId`, `miHudLess`, `v7Features`, ...) is converted with `npx @metricinsights/pp-dev migrate` (`--dry-run` to preview; a `.bak` copy is written).

## Next.js

`next.config.js` wraps the Next config with `withPPDev()` (`require` in a CommonJS project, `import` in an ESM one) and sets `output: 'export'`, `distDir: 'dist'` and `images.unoptimized: true`. `pp-dev next` serves the app under `/pl/<name>/` in development (API v7) and the export is served by MI under `/pt/<name>/`: import static assets in the code (Next applies the right `assetPrefix`) instead of hard-coding either prefix. `pp-dev next` restarts its server when `pp-dev.config.*`, `next.config.*` or `.env*` change.

## Dev server

- **Dev panel** in the page: sync the built template to MI (keeps up to `sync.maxBackups` backups of the page in `backupsDir`), open the Variables Editor (`/@pp-dev/variables-editor`) and the Request Inspector (`/@pp-dev/inspector`), work as other MI users (each saved user gets its own host, `<user>.localhost:<port>`).
- The dev server and its own routes answer `localhost`, `*.localhost` and IP hosts only; a tunnel's host name goes into `server.allowedHosts`.
- Personal access tokens authenticate to MI as the developer: keep them in `.env`, bind the server to `localhost` unless another device needs it.

# Working with Variables
Variables must be created on the Metric Insights server tied to App development. Variables are instantiated in the React application via the index.html file specifically

Variables in /index.html like:
```
<script>
    window.PP_VARIABLES = {
      TEST: '[test]',
      TEST_NUMBER: [testNumber]
    }
</script>
```

For example, a full implemantion might look like this (excerpt only includes body tag and its children)

```
<body>
    <div id="root"></div>
    <script>
      window.PP_VARIABLES = {
        ANNOUNCEMENT_ID: '[Announcement]',
        CONNECT_PAGE_BACKGROUND: '[Connect Page Background]',
        CONNECT_PAGE_TITLE: '[Connect Page Title]',
        CONNECT_PAGE_SUBTITLE: '[Connect Page Subtitle]',
        CONNECT_PAGE_TILES: [Connect Page Tiles],
        SIDEBAR_LOGO: '[Sidebar Logo]',
        GLOSSARY_DATASET: '[Glossary Dataset]',
        STACK_ELEMENTS_DATASET: '[Stack Elements Dataset]',
        CUSTOM_FIELDS_DATASET: '[Custom Fields Dataset]',
        CUSTOM_PERSONA_PAGE_ACCESS_DATASET: '[Custom Personas Page Access]',
        CUSTOM_PERSONA_VISUAL_ACCESS_DATASET: '[Custom Personas Visual Access]',
        CUSTOM_PERSONA_PAGE_INFO_DATASET: '[Custom Personas Pages Dataset]',
        CUSTOM_PERSONA_PAGE_CORE_METRICS_DATASET: '[Custom Personas Page Core Metrics]',
        CUSTOM_PERSONA_VISUALS_DATASET: '[Custom Personas Visuals]',
        POWER_BI_ELEMENT: '[Power BI element]',
        POWER_BI_ELEMENTS: '[Power BI Reports]',
        MAX_CUSTOM_PAGE_METRIC_TITLE: '[Max Page Metrics Title]',
        MAX_CUSTOM_PAGE_METRIC_TEXT: '[Max Page Metrics Msg]',
        CUSTOM_PERSONA_VISUAL_WIDTH: '[Custom Persona Visual Width]',
        CUSTOM_PERSONA_VISUAL_HEIGHT: '[Custom Persona Visual Height]',
        MOBILE_CUSTOM_PERSONA_VISUAL_HEIGHT: '[Mobile Custom Persona Visual Height]',
      };
    </script>
    <script type="module" src="/src/main.tsx"></script>
  </body>
  ```